       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum dose. It could seriously harm the patient, and you've said you aren't a clinician, so the order needs a licensed prescriber behind it.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the standard range.** The usual range is 25\u2013200 mg once daily. Give me the intended dose and I'll enter it.\n- **Route the request to the right person.** The treating physician or another licensed prescriber can contact pharmacy directly if they think an unusual dose is clinically justified. Pharmacy can then verify it through the hospital's high-alert medication process.\n\nIf this is a test of the order system, tell me and I can help in another way. I won't place the 1000 mg order itself."
